<title>BELGIUM: Generale Bank cuts Royale Belge to sell.</title>
<headline>Generale Bank cuts Royale Belge to sell.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Generale Bank said it was cutting Royale Belge to &quot;sell&quot; from &quot;hold&quot; after the insurer's sharp rise in the past days on speculation of a closer link with the AXA-UAP group.</p>
<p>&quot;At current levels the valuation of the stock reflects the good fundamentals and includes a speculative premium about a possible buyout by AXA-UAP of Group Frere's stake in RB,&quot; Generale Bank said in an investor note. &quot;At this stage we think it is too early to speculate on how a merger might work.&quot;</p>
<p>Generale Bank noted Royale Belge has risen 39.8 percent this year while the Bel-20 leading stock index is up 14.5 percent.</p>
<p>-- Nick Antonovics, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6817, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
